    "title": "Project 1",
    "year": "2022",
    "image": "../images/project1.png",
    "description": "I explored how the macro-nutritional composition of sausage and bacon products changes as price increases. By analyzing price per calorie, I found that as products become more expensive, they tend to be leaner. Protein increases while fat decreases. To highlight this relationship, I grouped products into equally sized price bins and graphed the average macronutrient proportion using a smoothed line chart. This made it easy to pinpoint when the two macronutrients crossed over, or when protein overtook fat, emphasizing how higher-priced options shift toward higher protein content."
